action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P94 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): a TextEditor undoes one change at a time.
#   TEST_BACKEND=gtk4 zsh testapp/test.zsh P94 --macos --actionfile testapp/actions/mac/P94-undo-gtk4.actions
# The editor starts as "hello". GTK joined two pastes into one undo step; the framework keeps
# the history for a GtkTextView too since 2026-10-14 (GtkBackend+TextUndo.swift). Keys only.
# The clipboard is used: it ends holding "hello".
# Expected "editor" lines in p94-undo.log, in order (an empty one is "editor "):
#   "" hello hellohello | hello "" hello | "" hello | helloa helloab helloabc | helloab hello | helloab
# The fourth Undo has nothing left and must add no line. a and b are typed together and are
# one step; c comes 1.5 s later and is its own.
# macOS 上 GtkBackend 的 P94:TextEditor 一次復原一個變更。編輯器起始為 hello;只用按鍵;會用到剪貼簿，結束時內容是
# hello。p94-undo.log 的 editor 各行應依序如上;第四次 Undo 不得多出一行;a 與 b 連打算一步，c 隔 1.5 秒自成一步。
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let the window settle,macos
